    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10119" root="خدع" body-key="x">
    
      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خادعهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَادَعَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِدَاعٌ</span>: see 1, in
five places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَادَعَةٌ العَيْنِ</span> means <i>The causing
the eye to doubt respecting that which it sees.</i>
(Ham p. 541.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خادع المَجْدَ</span>, (As, K, *) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَمْدَ</span>, (AA,) a phrase used by Er-Rá'ee, (TA,)
<i>He forsook,</i> or <i>relinquished,</i> (As, AA, K,) <i>glory,</i>
(As,) or <i>praise,</i> not being worthy of it. (AA.)

